WEBVTT

00:27.193 --> 00:29.320
Masumi.

00:29.988 --> 00:31.281
Stop that.

00:31.865 --> 00:33.950
Don't touch dead things.

00:50.383 --> 00:51.217
Hello.

00:51.718 --> 00:53.887
This is Medical Examiner Japan.

00:58.266 --> 01:00.351
Thank you for coming. It's this way.

01:00.977 --> 01:02.979
Yasuo Izawa, 52-year-old male.

01:03.063 --> 01:04.314
Found lying face up

01:04.397 --> 01:07.358
on this road around 1:00 a.m. today
after being hit by a truck.

01:07.442 --> 01:09.527
A passerby called emergency services.

01:09.611 --> 01:14.032
When they arrived, they concluded
he had already passed away.

01:14.115 --> 01:17.702
That man over there is the first witness,
Nobuhiko Yamanuki.

01:17.786 --> 01:20.705
His company handles transportation
for Mr. Izawa's factory.

01:20.789 --> 01:22.999
At our company,
we're all part of a family…

01:23.083 --> 01:25.919
It seems they were somewhat
acquainted through work.

01:27.545 --> 01:28.588
What?

01:28.671 --> 01:29.798
Doctor?

01:32.592 --> 01:35.011
Is this car paint?

01:35.094 --> 01:36.221
Paint fragments?

01:37.430 --> 01:40.308
The same paint is on him here.

01:40.391 --> 01:42.852
There are broken glass fragments
over here too.

01:43.978 --> 01:46.189
Does this mean he was hit by a car?

01:46.272 --> 01:48.191
-Probably.
-No.

01:48.274 --> 01:50.735
We can't be sure of that yet
with just this.

01:50.819 --> 01:53.238
This is near Mr. Izawa's home.

01:53.321 --> 01:56.407
It's believed he was in an accident
while on his way back.

01:57.909 --> 01:59.494
Were there no witnesses?

01:59.577 --> 02:01.121
None so far.

02:01.204 --> 02:04.165
However,
Mr. Izawa's smartphone is missing.

02:04.249 --> 02:06.876
The perpetrator likely took it.

02:07.836 --> 02:09.921
To prevent him from calling for help?

02:10.004 --> 02:11.089
Presumably.

02:11.172 --> 02:12.507
Presumably.

02:12.590 --> 02:14.801
With the scene in mind,

02:14.884 --> 02:17.262
this doesn't look like
a simple traffic accident.

02:18.596 --> 02:19.722
Doctor?

02:19.806 --> 02:21.099
What is it?

02:22.475 --> 02:25.645
The estimated point of impact
based on the paint fragments,

02:25.728 --> 02:28.565
and Mr. Izawa's position
are too close together.

02:28.648 --> 02:29.983
What do you mean?

02:30.066 --> 02:32.235
In a collision with a vehicle,

02:32.318 --> 02:35.029
a person would normally
be thrown further away.

02:35.113 --> 02:36.906
No matter how small the car is,

02:36.990 --> 02:40.118
you are hitting a mass of steel
weighing over 300 kilograms.

02:41.035 --> 02:41.911
It doesn't add up.

02:41.995 --> 02:43.788
You can't say for certain

02:43.872 --> 02:46.416
that these fragments fell
at the moment of impact.

02:46.499 --> 02:50.753
But you could also say that they did.

02:50.837 --> 02:52.797
In other words, it's a mystery.

02:54.048 --> 02:55.425
There's one more issue.

02:55.508 --> 02:56.801
Huh? What is it?

02:56.885 --> 02:58.428
Acceleration marks.

03:01.055 --> 03:04.183
These are marks left
when a car accelerates.

03:04.267 --> 03:06.144
The presence of acceleration marks

03:06.227 --> 03:09.689
implies the car hit Mr. Izawa
at a high speed.

03:09.772 --> 03:13.276
In that case,
he should have landed further away.

03:13.359 --> 03:16.070
So what's your point?

03:17.405 --> 03:19.949
For now, it's a mystery.

03:20.700 --> 03:22.285
-So--
-All right, all right.

03:22.368 --> 03:24.245
I get it, I get it.

03:40.470 --> 03:41.679
Let's begin.

03:51.689 --> 03:55.818
There are signs of bruising
on the back of the head and shoulders.

03:55.902 --> 03:59.864
But I don't believe
this was the fatal blow.

03:59.948 --> 04:04.786
There are also marks on the thigh
resembling a bumper impact,

04:04.869 --> 04:08.039
but that is also unlikely
to be the cause of death.

04:08.122 --> 04:10.124
Upon opening the retroperitoneum,

04:10.208 --> 04:13.086
the tissue around the pelvis
was found to be completely blackened.

04:13.169 --> 04:18.299
The pelvis was severely fractured,
causing massive internal bleeding.

04:18.383 --> 04:21.886
So the cause of death
was internal bleeding?

04:21.970 --> 04:22.804
Yes.

04:22.887 --> 04:26.057
I believe Mr. Izawa's cause of death
was hemorrhagic shock

04:26.140 --> 04:28.017
due to a pelvic fracture.

04:28.101 --> 04:31.437
Well, at least it seems certain
it was a traffic accident.

04:31.521 --> 04:35.066
In a traffic accident,
a person reflexively tries

04:35.149 --> 04:37.902
to protect their body with their arms
at the moment of impact.

04:37.986 --> 04:42.532
Naturally, defense wounds
would remain on one of the arms.

04:42.615 --> 04:44.617
However, in Mr. Izawa's case,

04:44.701 --> 04:46.661
there are none.

04:46.744 --> 04:47.954
It doesn't add up.

04:48.037 --> 04:50.248
That is certainly unnatural.

04:50.331 --> 04:52.750
There are not enough injuries
for a collision.

04:52.834 --> 04:55.211
Usually, there are skin tears.

04:55.295 --> 04:56.629
And yet,

04:56.713 --> 04:59.257
there's only one cut
on the back of his hand.

04:59.340 --> 05:00.591
You're right.

05:03.052 --> 05:06.097
The pieces of the puzzle
may be coming together.

05:07.140 --> 05:11.269
If Mr. Izawa's death
was caused by a car collision,

05:11.352 --> 05:13.813
and the pelvic fracture…

05:14.647 --> 05:18.151
Then he must have been hit
by a car moving extremely slowly.

05:18.234 --> 05:20.361
For now, it's a mystery.

05:20.445 --> 05:21.487
-What?
-What?

05:21.571 --> 05:24.115
-What do you mean?
-What do you mean?

05:24.198 --> 05:25.283
Come back…

05:25.366 --> 05:26.743
Yes, excuse me.

05:27.327 --> 05:29.037
Your turn, Dr. Takamori.

05:29.620 --> 05:30.455
Okay.

05:32.582 --> 05:33.541
First,

05:33.624 --> 05:36.419
when hit by a fast car,

05:36.502 --> 05:40.715
you are thrown a significant distance
and suffer various external injuries.

05:41.632 --> 05:45.011
But if hit by a very slow car,

05:45.094 --> 05:46.971
you fall straight backward.

05:47.472 --> 05:49.265
Like a heavy fall on your rear.

05:49.932 --> 05:52.894
In this case, the force is focused
on the center of the body,

05:52.977 --> 05:54.729
which can cause a pelvic fracture.

05:54.812 --> 05:57.982
I see. That would explain
why there are external injuries,

05:58.066 --> 06:00.443
but a severe internal one.

06:00.526 --> 06:01.611
Hang on a second.

06:02.361 --> 06:04.781
How slow is "slow"?

06:08.826 --> 06:10.286
About 20 kilometers per hour?

06:10.369 --> 06:13.956
You can easily avoid a car
moving that slowly, can't you?

06:14.040 --> 06:17.168
At the very least,
it wouldn't be a direct hit.

06:17.251 --> 06:19.128
Then maybe he was hit intentionally?

06:19.212 --> 06:21.631
Don't you think that's a bit of a stretch?

06:21.714 --> 06:22.924
That's right!

06:24.383 --> 06:26.928
Doctor, what do you think?

06:27.637 --> 06:28.471
Well…

06:31.140 --> 06:33.726
If the vehicle was moving fast,

06:33.810 --> 06:35.853
it contradicts the body's distance.

06:35.937 --> 06:38.189
If the vehicle was moving slowly,

06:38.272 --> 06:41.192
there should not be
any acceleration marks.

06:41.275 --> 06:45.113
Several points don't add up,
whether it moved slowly or fast.

06:45.196 --> 06:48.783
And, the lack of defense wounds
remains unexplained.

06:48.866 --> 06:50.952
Considering all of this…

06:53.287 --> 06:54.622
Considering all of that?

06:57.333 --> 06:59.502
For now, it's a mystery.

07:17.186 --> 07:18.020
Yes?

07:20.606 --> 07:21.441
What?

07:24.902 --> 07:26.279
I understand.

07:28.406 --> 07:29.490
Was that Dojima?

07:30.199 --> 07:31.033
Yes.

07:31.117 --> 07:32.952
It seems they found the truck driver.

07:33.035 --> 07:35.037
I would like to hear what he has to say.

07:35.121 --> 07:36.247
Wait, Doctor…

07:37.165 --> 07:39.167
Well, about that…

07:47.884 --> 07:50.428
The deceased is Kazutoshi Tamura,
24 years old.

07:50.511 --> 07:53.055
He was the driver
of the truck in the incident.

07:53.139 --> 07:56.309
A missing person's report
was filed by his transport company.

07:56.392 --> 07:59.854
We confirmed he was using the truck
on the day of the incident.

08:03.024 --> 08:04.859
Anything catch your eye?

08:06.527 --> 08:07.528
Where's the truck?

08:07.612 --> 08:09.906
It was abandoned nearby.

08:14.785 --> 08:17.413
The bumper is dented,
and the paint is chipped.

08:19.624 --> 08:23.127
Mr. Izawa's smartphone
was found in the deceased's pocket.

08:23.211 --> 08:24.253
What?

08:24.337 --> 08:25.963
And on top of that.

08:28.341 --> 08:30.968
This was found in his pocket as well.

08:31.052 --> 08:32.220
The police think

08:32.303 --> 08:35.389
it was a suicide motivated
by remorse over the hit-and-run.

08:40.895 --> 08:44.232
The driver suspected of the hit-and-run

08:44.899 --> 08:47.443
was found dead by hanging.

08:52.865 --> 08:54.909
So he killed my husband

08:56.410 --> 08:59.080
and then just took
the easy way out for himself?

09:02.041 --> 09:03.918
How could this happen?

09:06.963 --> 09:09.924
I understand how you feel.

09:13.511 --> 09:18.641
Do you recognize this man named Tamura?

09:19.809 --> 09:22.228
Anything at all will help.

09:24.438 --> 09:28.734
He has come to our factory a few times.

09:30.444 --> 09:33.447
I think he was in charge
of our deliveries.

09:35.074 --> 09:39.495
Did you notice anything
strange about their relationship?

09:41.414 --> 09:42.498
One time,

09:42.582 --> 09:46.877
I saw the two of them having an argument.

09:47.503 --> 09:50.756
Do you know what it was about?

09:52.008 --> 09:54.635
I couldn't hear any details.

09:54.719 --> 09:59.473
When I asked my husband
if he was all right,

10:00.099 --> 10:02.226
I got no clear answer.

10:03.185 --> 10:07.231
Would you say they were
on bad terms with each other?

10:08.816 --> 10:09.859
No.

10:09.942 --> 10:11.360
I don't think they were.

10:13.279 --> 10:17.074
Did they often meet with each other?

10:20.411 --> 10:22.872
I don't know any details, but…

10:23.581 --> 10:27.293
I think they met a few times every month.

10:29.837 --> 10:31.964
Thank you.

10:37.428 --> 10:39.305
He hits him with his truck,

10:39.388 --> 10:41.932
and then commits suicide over the guilt.

10:42.516 --> 10:44.018
That's the size of it, right?

10:44.101 --> 10:46.687
We don't currently know.

10:47.396 --> 10:51.233
If they had some bad blood
between each other for whatever reason,

10:51.317 --> 10:54.695
then it's a possibility he hit him
with his truck on purpose, isn't it?

10:55.529 --> 10:59.367
We don't currently know that either.

11:00.451 --> 11:02.078
You're right.

11:02.828 --> 11:03.913
Sorry.

11:04.538 --> 11:07.208
However,
there is one thing that caught my eye.

11:08.167 --> 11:09.001
What is it?

11:09.085 --> 11:12.380
The condition of Tamura's body
at the scene.

11:12.463 --> 11:15.299
Normally, when one dies
from asphyxiation from hanging,

11:15.383 --> 11:17.385
their face becomes pale.

11:17.468 --> 11:21.514
However, Tamura's complexion
looked just fine.

11:21.597 --> 11:24.141
He had all the color in his face, right?

11:24.225 --> 11:25.309
Yes.

11:25.893 --> 11:26.811
Therefore…

11:33.734 --> 11:34.777
Let's begin.

11:43.702 --> 11:44.870
It's over here!

11:46.372 --> 11:49.125
YAMANUKI SHIPPING CO., LTD.

11:49.208 --> 11:54.004
Could you tell us about
how Kazutoshi Tamura was at work?

11:54.588 --> 11:55.714
Right…

11:55.798 --> 11:57.133
Tamura…

11:59.135 --> 12:03.055
It honestly pains me
to speak ill of the dead.

12:03.139 --> 12:04.974
Were there any problems?

12:06.183 --> 12:09.228
He was often found sleeping
in the middle of work.

12:09.311 --> 12:10.646
Are you okay?

12:11.272 --> 12:12.189
Sorry.

12:12.815 --> 12:14.442
He was not very bright.

12:17.111 --> 12:18.237
What are you doing?

12:18.320 --> 12:21.490
To be honest,
I wasn't sure what to do about him.

12:23.784 --> 12:25.578
I didn't really want to do this,

12:25.661 --> 12:28.205
but I attached a GPS to his truck
to monitor him.

12:28.289 --> 12:30.082
A GPS…

12:30.166 --> 12:33.252
We also have the shift records over there.

12:33.335 --> 12:36.130
-Please look at them if needed.
-Thank you very much.

12:45.514 --> 12:46.348
Hey.

12:46.432 --> 12:47.475
Yes, sorry!

12:52.271 --> 12:55.816
There was mild pulmonary edema
in his lungs.

12:56.734 --> 12:59.528
This can be a sign of asphyxiation,

12:59.612 --> 13:03.115
but also a sign of heart failure
or death from poisoning.

13:03.199 --> 13:04.825
The CT scan results show

13:04.909 --> 13:07.244
that the decisive blow
wasn't to the heart or brain.

13:07.328 --> 13:08.913
It doesn't seem like heart failure.

13:08.996 --> 13:10.331
Thank you.

13:10.998 --> 13:12.833
Next, on the neck,

13:12.917 --> 13:16.295
there are clear rope marks left.

13:16.378 --> 13:18.464
So, he died by hanging?

13:18.547 --> 13:21.425
We can't draw a conclusion just from that.

13:21.509 --> 13:23.594
Because you can make it look like

13:23.677 --> 13:26.305
someone hanged themselves
after killing them, right?

13:26.388 --> 13:27.515
Yes.

13:27.598 --> 13:31.810
There is one more thing
that caught my eye during the autopsy.

13:32.478 --> 13:33.938
Thank you for your cooperation.

13:34.021 --> 13:35.898
No, I'm happy to help with this.

13:35.981 --> 13:37.399
Well then, goodbye.

13:38.108 --> 13:39.652
By the way…

13:41.487 --> 13:45.074
you wouldn't know about any trouble
Izawa was having, would you?

13:45.157 --> 13:46.575
Trouble?

13:47.368 --> 13:49.119
Trouble…

13:49.203 --> 13:50.079
Well…

13:50.162 --> 13:51.372
Did you think of something?

13:51.455 --> 13:53.290
Well, it's only a rumor.

13:53.374 --> 13:55.125
Only a rumor?

13:55.209 --> 13:56.627
Actually…

13:59.463 --> 14:00.714
Take a look at this.

14:01.507 --> 14:04.176
There are few petechial hemorrhages
behind the eyes.

14:04.260 --> 14:05.886
In cases of asphyxiation,

14:05.970 --> 14:09.014
blood that should flow down
from the neck pools,

14:09.098 --> 14:12.101
and there should be
signs of bleeding behind the eyes.

14:12.184 --> 14:14.770
If it wasn't hanging, then what was it?

14:15.396 --> 14:18.148
We're still missing some pieces.

14:19.900 --> 14:21.986
How was the autopsy for Kazutoshi Tamura?

14:22.069 --> 14:23.320
How was it?

14:23.404 --> 14:26.532
We couldn't conclude
that Tamura's cause of death was hanging.

14:26.615 --> 14:27.783
I see.

14:27.867 --> 14:29.076
What about you?

14:30.077 --> 14:31.662
We learned something interesting.

14:32.997 --> 14:37.543
Izawa had been in debt
for two years to run the factory.

14:37.626 --> 14:39.336
Nearly 100 million yen.

14:39.420 --> 14:40.838
What? 100 million?

14:40.921 --> 14:41.922
That's not all.

14:42.006 --> 14:45.342
A 100 million yen life insurance policy
was taken out on Izawa.

14:45.426 --> 14:48.596
And it's only been three months
since he signed it.

14:48.679 --> 14:51.307
I see it as money to protect the company.

14:51.390 --> 14:55.185
The police are moving forward with
the investigation as a case

14:55.269 --> 14:57.187
of induced suicide by Akemi Izawa.

14:57.688 --> 15:00.441
Wait, what does that mean?

15:01.400 --> 15:04.987
We mean that she induced Izawa
to commit suicide

15:05.070 --> 15:07.364
and make it look like an accident.

15:07.448 --> 15:10.242
To get the 100 million
from the life insurance policy.

15:10.326 --> 15:11.702
No, wait.

15:12.411 --> 15:13.454
If that's true,

15:13.537 --> 15:17.541
then why would the driver,
Tamura, have to die?

15:18.250 --> 15:22.671
If it's discovered he committed suicide,
then she won't get the 100 million.

15:22.755 --> 15:25.049
She killed the driver, Kazutoshi Tamura,

15:25.132 --> 15:28.052
and made it look like a suicide.

15:29.219 --> 15:32.348
Then it would make sense
that he didn't have much hemorrhaging

15:32.431 --> 15:35.142
because he didn't die of asphyxiation.

15:35.225 --> 15:39.605
That may also explain why Izawa
didn't dodge a slow-moving truck.

15:39.688 --> 15:41.982
Because she hesitated
to run over her husband,

15:42.066 --> 15:44.318
Akemi hit Mr. Izawa
at a half-hearted speed.

15:45.152 --> 15:47.488
Does that mean Akemi is the culprit?

15:47.571 --> 15:49.782
We'll go ask the suspect directly.

15:49.865 --> 15:52.451
Yes. We'll check with the insurance
company for--

15:52.534 --> 15:53.494
Don't dawdle!

15:53.577 --> 15:54.703
Yes, ma'am!

15:54.787 --> 15:56.163
I'll get the referral!

16:07.341 --> 16:08.384
Doctor,

16:09.093 --> 16:10.427
what do you think?

16:27.528 --> 16:29.738
The night of the accident?

16:29.822 --> 16:31.573
I was at home.

16:32.825 --> 16:35.285
I see.

16:35.953 --> 16:39.164
I'm under suspicion, aren't I?

16:40.124 --> 16:42.918
Oh, no, it's nothing like that.

16:44.253 --> 16:46.255
A police officer came by earlier, too,

16:47.131 --> 16:50.009
and asked me all sorts of things.

16:55.139 --> 16:58.517
Like about how managing the factory
wasn't going well,

16:59.476 --> 17:01.812
and about my husband's
life insurance money.

17:03.063 --> 17:08.694
I wonder if they think I killed him
for the insurance money.

17:09.361 --> 17:11.488
No, we're not saying that.

17:11.572 --> 17:14.033
Just because we have debts to pay back…

17:14.116 --> 17:17.661
I haven't fallen so low
as to commit murder.

17:20.122 --> 17:21.540
I'm very sorry.

17:23.500 --> 17:25.502
You have a child, huh?

17:30.049 --> 17:31.258
Yes.

17:32.092 --> 17:32.926
Well…

17:35.471 --> 17:36.722
Kazuki…

17:38.766 --> 17:41.727
passed away ten years ago.

17:44.980 --> 17:46.273
It was suicide.

17:48.984 --> 17:50.152
Kazuki

17:50.986 --> 17:52.112
was a serious boy.

17:53.322 --> 17:55.074
But he was clumsy,

17:55.157 --> 17:57.159
and everything he tried

17:57.242 --> 17:59.578
seemed to go nowhere.

18:01.330 --> 18:04.333
His job hunting didn't go well either.

18:10.756 --> 18:12.091
REJECTION NOTICE

18:12.174 --> 18:13.092
Kazuki.

18:13.759 --> 18:14.802
I'm coming in.

18:24.937 --> 18:26.814
Is it not going well?

18:29.399 --> 18:30.567
Dad, actually…

18:30.651 --> 18:31.527
What?

18:32.528 --> 18:36.323
Would it be okay
if I worked for your company?

18:38.992 --> 18:41.870
Even if you join us, you'll only suffer.

18:43.288 --> 18:45.791
Why don't you keep at it
just a little bit longer?

18:50.170 --> 18:53.674
My husband didn't really want
him to join the company,

18:55.843 --> 18:58.762
but to find a better job,

18:59.596 --> 19:01.974
and become happy.

19:07.229 --> 19:08.397
But that day…

19:09.022 --> 19:10.816
Kazuki, I'm coming in.

19:11.441 --> 19:12.568
I've got breakfast--

19:15.070 --> 19:17.781
It was my husband who found Kazuki

19:18.949 --> 19:20.284
after he had hanged himself.

19:26.915 --> 19:28.959
My husband thought that if only

19:30.002 --> 19:32.963
he had noticed Kazuki's
suffering back then, Kazuki would…

19:34.339 --> 19:37.342
My husband always blamed himself for it.

19:39.928 --> 19:41.013
Day…

19:43.515 --> 19:44.558
after day…

19:51.273 --> 19:54.443
I would never do such a thing.

20:02.117 --> 20:04.077
I don't think it's possible after all.

20:07.039 --> 20:09.917
I don't think someone
who cares so much for their family

20:10.751 --> 20:13.170
would commit instigation of suicide.

20:15.964 --> 20:21.345
You cannot conclude
whether a parent is truly

20:22.971 --> 20:24.556
thinking of their child.

20:49.831 --> 20:53.126
The doctor was kind of strange today.

20:53.835 --> 20:56.171
From what I know, he just seems like that.

20:57.297 --> 20:58.507
Well, yes.

20:59.216 --> 21:01.093
He's always calm and collected, right?

21:01.176 --> 21:02.844
He just does sudoku.

21:03.512 --> 21:04.388
Yeah.

21:05.097 --> 21:05.931
Oh.

21:06.431 --> 21:09.226
Maybe it's just not a topic
he's comfortable with.

21:10.227 --> 21:11.311
Not comfortable?

21:11.937 --> 21:14.690
Like parental love?
It's not that uncommon.

21:56.356 --> 21:59.526
I'm very sorry about the other day…

22:03.905 --> 22:07.993
I visited the factory,
but you weren't there.

22:08.827 --> 22:11.913
I've decided to close down the factory.

22:14.166 --> 22:17.169
The management
wasn't going well to begin with.

22:18.754 --> 22:20.672
And my husband is gone now, too.

22:34.311 --> 22:35.395
Ma'am,

22:36.480 --> 22:38.815
if it's all right with you,

22:38.899 --> 22:41.359
could we investigate inside the house?

22:43.028 --> 22:45.447
We might find some kind of clue.

22:51.495 --> 22:55.707
I want to find out exactly
what happened on the day of the incident.

22:57.167 --> 22:58.627
For your husband's sake.

23:01.838 --> 23:03.840
Above all, for your own sake.

23:10.972 --> 23:13.475
He's coming up from the rear!

23:13.558 --> 23:15.227
Go, go, go!

23:16.394 --> 23:18.021
-All right!
-Wow.

23:18.105 --> 23:19.439
You did it.

23:19.523 --> 23:20.482
What?

23:20.565 --> 23:21.650
Right.

23:23.652 --> 23:25.403
Is there anyone here

23:25.487 --> 23:29.825
who used the same truck
as the late Mr. Tamura?

23:30.784 --> 23:32.327
I have.

23:32.410 --> 23:33.829
-Great!
-Me too.

23:33.912 --> 23:34.788
Great!

23:35.497 --> 23:38.416
Have you felt unwell
in the past few weeks?

23:39.292 --> 23:41.002
Just a little dizzy.

23:41.086 --> 23:42.796
I had a cold.

23:44.381 --> 23:45.841
Thank you very much.

23:45.924 --> 23:48.677
There is something I would like to check.

23:49.928 --> 23:52.931
This is the truck
he was driving that night.

23:53.014 --> 23:54.349
Oh, I see.

23:58.395 --> 24:00.313
Oh, may I borrow this?

24:04.442 --> 24:06.903
Hey… Are you okay?

24:06.987 --> 24:09.114
Oh, don't worry.

24:17.205 --> 24:19.374
I'm sorry to be so forward.

24:19.457 --> 24:21.084
No…

24:27.591 --> 24:29.885
If I take anything that seems of interest,

24:29.968 --> 24:31.928
even if I don't understand what it is,

24:32.554 --> 24:35.390
Dr. Masumi might notice something.

24:38.894 --> 24:40.520
Well, in that case,

24:41.271 --> 24:44.482
would you like to check Kazuki's room too?

24:45.108 --> 24:46.193
What?

24:50.822 --> 24:51.990
This is it.

24:54.993 --> 24:59.497
We've left it just as it was
since Kazuki passed.

25:01.333 --> 25:02.792
Neither I nor my husband

25:03.460 --> 25:05.462
could quite accept it.

25:11.009 --> 25:12.427
If you would like,

25:13.595 --> 25:15.513
could you investigate it?

25:17.057 --> 25:17.891
Yes.

25:20.310 --> 25:21.603
Thank you very much.

25:24.272 --> 25:25.148
I'll go in then.

25:43.041 --> 25:45.043
I used to have one of these, too.

25:46.044 --> 25:48.922
When I first started working,
I tried to act like an adult.

25:51.299 --> 25:53.176
That fountain pen

25:53.927 --> 25:56.846
is something my husband
gave to Kazuki as a present.

25:57.847 --> 26:00.433
When his job hunting wasn't going well,

26:00.517 --> 26:02.936
he told him that if he used it
to write his resumes,

26:03.019 --> 26:04.187
he would be fine.

26:17.367 --> 26:18.535
I'm back!

26:18.618 --> 26:20.036
Ms. Kiryu, what's all that?

26:20.120 --> 26:22.205
I got permission from Akemi

26:22.289 --> 26:24.249
and borrowed some of his belongings.

26:24.332 --> 26:25.458
This much?

26:25.542 --> 26:26.418
Yes.

26:28.044 --> 26:28.962
Everyone.

26:29.045 --> 26:31.298
Could you help me investigate everything?

26:31.381 --> 26:33.341
How are we going to handle all this?

26:33.425 --> 26:35.927
I'm busy too, you know. I'll pass.

26:36.011 --> 26:37.053
Please.

26:37.679 --> 26:38.972
I'm asking you.

26:41.683 --> 26:43.435
Dr. Masumi, you too, please.

26:46.896 --> 26:49.691
I just can't believe Akemi is the culprit.

26:50.317 --> 26:54.404
So, I thought you might be able
to find some kind of clue.

26:56.489 --> 26:57.574
Please.

26:58.408 --> 26:59.659
Of course.

27:00.285 --> 27:01.578
Thank you very much.

27:02.579 --> 27:03.621
All right.

27:05.165 --> 27:07.250
You too, Dr. Matsubara.

27:07.334 --> 27:08.835
-Ugh.
-Come on.

27:08.918 --> 27:11.087
I've got a show I want to watch!

27:11.171 --> 27:12.922
Just record it, then.

27:14.507 --> 27:15.759
Here, thank you.

27:18.678 --> 27:19.512
All right.

27:24.225 --> 27:25.101
Hey.

27:25.894 --> 27:30.273
This is a gift Izawa gave to Kazuki
when he was job hunting.

27:38.198 --> 27:40.450
-What were Tamura's blood test results?
-Hold on.

27:40.950 --> 27:41.910
Where are they…

27:43.703 --> 27:44.746
Here.

27:46.498 --> 27:47.957
Acetaminophen.

27:50.794 --> 27:52.545
What is that?

27:53.546 --> 27:56.466
It's an ingredient often found
in things like cold medicine.

28:06.935 --> 28:08.311
You can make it look like

28:08.395 --> 28:09.979
someone hanged themselves…

28:10.063 --> 28:11.356
…no defense wounds.

28:11.439 --> 28:13.149
There's only one cut
on the back of his hand.

28:13.233 --> 28:14.442
Just a little dizzy.

28:14.526 --> 28:15.860
I had a cold.

28:15.944 --> 28:18.696
Kazuki passed away ten years ago.

28:18.780 --> 28:21.741
This is a gift Izawa gave to Kazuki
when he was job hunting.

28:21.825 --> 28:23.451
Acetaminophen.

28:23.535 --> 28:26.246
I think they met a few times every month.

28:41.720 --> 28:43.263
The pieces may be

28:45.181 --> 28:47.225
coming together.

29:03.992 --> 29:06.745
MUSASHINODAI POLICE OFFICE

29:14.461 --> 29:17.672
Thank you for coming while you're so busy.

29:17.756 --> 29:20.842
There is something
I would like to ask you about.

29:21.342 --> 29:23.595
I'm sorry, but I'm busy,

29:23.678 --> 29:26.055
so could we finish this
as quickly as possible?

29:27.098 --> 29:28.099
I understand.

29:36.274 --> 29:37.108
Right this way.

29:40.445 --> 29:41.613
Please, have a seat here.

29:41.696 --> 29:42.530
Okay.

29:45.700 --> 29:51.164
These are photos taken
when I visited your company the other day.

29:53.625 --> 29:55.627
You can't just take liberties like that.

29:55.710 --> 29:57.378
I'm terribly sorry.

29:58.046 --> 30:01.508
I just had something
that was bothering me.

30:04.594 --> 30:07.597
This is the truck Tamura
drove on the night of the incident.

30:07.680 --> 30:09.265
Please look at this part.

30:09.349 --> 30:10.975
The pipe is broken.

30:11.726 --> 30:16.189
Also, there are cracks in the welding
several centimeters big.

30:18.316 --> 30:21.277
And there is one more thing
that concerns me.

30:24.280 --> 30:27.700
Tamura had been suffering from symptoms

30:27.784 --> 30:31.079
like dizziness and a cold
for several weeks.

30:31.162 --> 30:32.539
Strangely,

30:33.206 --> 30:38.336
there were several others
suffering from similar symptoms.

30:38.419 --> 30:40.338
It's just a coincidence.

30:40.421 --> 30:42.632
Everyone at our company works hard,

30:42.715 --> 30:45.218
so it wouldn't be strange
for them to fall ill.

30:46.636 --> 30:50.849
I do not believe
that it was a coincidence.

30:52.475 --> 30:54.018
On what grounds?

30:54.602 --> 30:56.229
I believe the workers

30:56.312 --> 31:01.192
were suffering from
carbon monoxide poisoning.

31:03.361 --> 31:05.405
On the day of the incident,

31:05.488 --> 31:07.490
Tamura parked the truck on the street,

31:07.574 --> 31:11.411
and exhausted from working all day,
took a nap.

31:12.912 --> 31:14.038
That day,

31:14.122 --> 31:16.624
it was very humid,
even when the sun went down.

31:17.876 --> 31:21.588
He most likely left the air conditioner on
while inside the vehicle.

31:22.922 --> 31:26.593
If you continue to run it
while parked for a long time,

31:27.385 --> 31:32.724
exhaust gas will begin to accumulate
under the vehicle from that broken pipe.

31:33.766 --> 31:35.268
As a result,

31:35.351 --> 31:37.604
carbon monoxide,
which is lighter than air,

31:37.687 --> 31:42.650
leaked through the crack
in the bottom of the vehicle.

31:44.152 --> 31:47.697
Tamura, who was sleep-deprived,
had fallen into a deep sleep.

31:47.780 --> 31:51.367
And without even realizing it himself,

31:51.868 --> 31:54.787
he was suffering
from carbon monoxide poisoning.

31:55.830 --> 32:00.585
The reason his complexion looked normal
when his body was found

32:00.668 --> 32:02.295
was because of that.

32:04.464 --> 32:07.592
But what was more decisive than anything…

32:09.677 --> 32:10.762
was this.

32:12.764 --> 32:14.349
I'M SORRY FOR BEING LIKE THIS

32:15.308 --> 32:19.228
This note,
found at the scene of the incident.

32:20.647 --> 32:22.023
And that alone

32:23.816 --> 32:25.318
doesn't add up.

32:25.401 --> 32:26.527
What?

32:27.278 --> 32:28.529
Why?

32:31.032 --> 32:35.954
Initially, we thought this note
was a suicide note left by the driver,

32:36.037 --> 32:37.664
Kazutoshi Tamura.

32:39.832 --> 32:41.209
But we were wrong.

32:43.127 --> 32:45.046
What do you mean?

32:47.090 --> 32:49.384
It was written by your late son.

32:51.636 --> 32:52.804
What…

32:53.721 --> 32:58.309
These letters haven't bled
through to the back of the paper.

32:59.227 --> 33:03.272
The ink has not been absorbed
into the paper.

33:03.982 --> 33:05.775
If it were oil-based,
it would bleed through.

33:06.275 --> 33:09.862
If it were water-based,
it should smudge because of the paper.

33:10.405 --> 33:12.782
But it is neither of those.

33:13.408 --> 33:17.412
Pigmented gel ink is what it's called.

33:17.495 --> 33:20.039
Pigmented gel ink?

33:20.123 --> 33:26.170
Can you see the fine cracks in the ink
on the surface of these letters?

33:26.671 --> 33:30.174
A characteristic of pigmented gel ink
is that it cracks

33:30.258 --> 33:33.219
after several years of exposure to air.

33:33.720 --> 33:36.097
In other words, that means

33:36.180 --> 33:41.227
this note was written several years ago.

33:43.146 --> 33:44.772
And this ink

33:44.856 --> 33:46.482
matches the fountain pen

33:46.566 --> 33:51.446
that Izawa's son, Kazuki, used to love.

33:53.364 --> 33:55.992
I believe your husband
kept it with him at all times

33:56.701 --> 34:00.496
as a form of atonement.

34:04.584 --> 34:06.586
Why would something Kazuki wrote

34:07.253 --> 34:08.963
be inside the truck?

34:09.881 --> 34:11.174
I believe…

34:13.051 --> 34:15.762
your husband was trying to help Tamura.

34:20.725 --> 34:23.644
That night, when Izawa was going home…

34:24.479 --> 34:25.438
Hey!

34:25.521 --> 34:27.023
Are you sleeping?

34:27.940 --> 34:30.026
You'll catch a cold!

34:31.319 --> 34:32.153
Hey!

34:32.236 --> 34:34.822
Hey, are you okay? Hey!

34:49.504 --> 34:50.880
Hey, what's wrong?

34:50.963 --> 34:53.299
Hey! Pull yourself together!

34:53.382 --> 34:55.426
Hey!

34:56.427 --> 34:57.261
Hey…

34:57.345 --> 34:58.262
All right…

34:59.764 --> 35:04.560
Izawa inhaled carbon monoxide
from the vehicle.

35:12.235 --> 35:15.279
Is that bastard
seriously slacking off again?

35:27.875 --> 35:28.751
Hey!

35:29.710 --> 35:30.878
What happened?

35:34.507 --> 35:35.675
The truck…

35:37.135 --> 35:38.719
Something's wrong with it.

35:38.803 --> 35:40.138
What?

35:40.221 --> 35:41.806
I'm so dizzy.

35:54.694 --> 35:55.528
Hey.

35:56.445 --> 35:57.446
Are you okay?

35:58.698 --> 36:00.825
If this gets out, my company is ruined.

36:01.617 --> 36:03.119
Hey…

36:04.120 --> 36:05.246
Are you okay?

36:06.080 --> 36:07.039
Can you stand?

36:07.665 --> 36:09.458
I finally climbed my way to the top…

37:05.890 --> 37:08.851
And, after that, Yamanuki…

37:13.022 --> 37:15.274
I'M SORRY FOR BEING LIKE THIS

37:18.444 --> 37:21.656
He was desperately trying
to make it look like an accident.

37:26.619 --> 37:28.412
He put Tamura into the truck,

37:28.913 --> 37:30.081
and fled the scene.

37:42.885 --> 37:45.179
Tamura made it look like
he committed suicide.

37:48.891 --> 37:51.602
Considering the above,

37:53.271 --> 37:57.400
I believe the reason Yasuo Izawa
had no defensive wounds

37:58.526 --> 38:05.533
was that he was trying to protect Tamura,
who was unconscious at the time.

38:10.037 --> 38:13.207
If you had called an ambulance right then,

38:15.167 --> 38:18.879
they would both have survived.

38:23.551 --> 38:24.844
Neither of them…

38:27.221 --> 38:29.307
would have lost their lives.

38:34.854 --> 38:36.897
This is what we believe

38:38.065 --> 38:42.361
to have happened to Yasuo Izawa
on that day.

38:48.868 --> 38:49.994
My husband…

38:52.246 --> 38:55.583
tried to save someone?

38:58.711 --> 38:59.670
Yes.

39:03.299 --> 39:07.136
He tried to save Tamura,
who was about the same age as your son.

39:09.597 --> 39:11.307
He risked his life to do it.

39:28.032 --> 39:29.367
I…

39:31.285 --> 39:33.287
think he was a magnificent person.

39:46.050 --> 39:48.928
Detective! Please listen to me!
This man is--

39:49.011 --> 39:53.099
Overworking employees,
false statements, tampering with evidence…

39:53.182 --> 39:55.851
Plus a whole bunch of further offenses.

39:57.520 --> 40:00.272
Nobuhiko Yamanuki, you are under arrest

40:00.356 --> 40:02.608
for murder and failure to render aid.

40:04.944 --> 40:06.070
It looks like

40:06.153 --> 40:09.907
you're going to spend a lot of time
with us, don't you think?

40:11.742 --> 40:12.827
Let's go.

40:16.789 --> 40:17.748
Move!

40:18.416 --> 40:21.919
Thank you for your cooperation.

40:23.712 --> 40:25.005
You as well.

40:31.345 --> 40:32.430
Thank you,

40:33.180 --> 40:34.473
as always.

40:40.312 --> 40:41.480
From here on,

40:42.773 --> 40:44.650
it's police business, so…

41:02.251 --> 41:05.963
IZAWA

42:00.726 --> 42:05.105
I hope Izawa's feelings reached those two.

42:08.234 --> 42:12.029
Oh. From a forensic science
perspective, the deceased are…

42:12.112 --> 42:13.906
Yes, I get it.

42:21.956 --> 42:23.749
Thank you for today.

42:23.832 --> 42:25.125
Good work.

42:27.711 --> 42:29.046
Wait, Doctor.

42:29.129 --> 42:32.174
That reminds me.
I've actually wanted to ask you…

42:32.258 --> 42:35.594
Why did you want to become
a forensic pathologist?

42:37.680 --> 42:40.558
Well, I wonder why.

42:40.641 --> 42:43.143
For now, it's a mystery.

42:47.273 --> 42:48.732
Good work today.

43:02.329 --> 43:03.289
Masumi.

43:04.790 --> 43:06.083
Stop that.

43:07.042 --> 43:08.752
Don't touch dead things.

43:13.465 --> 43:14.633
Why…

43:17.845 --> 43:19.054
Dad?

43:19.680 --> 43:21.348
KOICHI MIZUSAWA

43:22.891 --> 43:24.435
There is no value

43:25.227 --> 43:26.353
in dead things.

43:40.326 --> 43:43.662
THIRD KILLING BY STRANGULATION THIS YEAR

43:44.496 --> 43:47.541
4TH CASE OF WOMAN FOUND STRANGLED

43:47.625 --> 43:50.919
SHIRAMINE SERIAL FEMICIDE CASE
RESEARCH DATA

43:53.297 --> 43:56.258
AUTOPSY REPORT

43:56.342 --> 43:59.678
SURGEON: MASAHITO KUJO
MARCH 2008

44:01.055 --> 44:04.141
ASSISTANT: MASUMI MIZUSAWA

44:04.224 --> 44:06.477
MASUMI MIZUSAWA

44:17.446 --> 44:20.866
Subtitle translation by: Maslin F.
